# Phase 5 T-U2 (the Ctrl-O reading position across a page rebuild, fx
# 026a8f4e, b1a53b01), mid-document: p5-transcript-anchor with one page up
# only. While the view is up, the command settles (its heading loses a row),
# a `* network:` record lands above the view and the answer lands below; row
# 1 of `full-pgup` and `full-pgup-after` says whether the view held. `end` is
# Ctrl-O again at the tail, where the settled `Ran` heading fits one row.
# fx's `shell`/`run` is xfx's `terminal`/`exec`; TZ=UTC on both (T-U5).
fx: gateway p5-transcript-anchor-turns.json
xfx: gateway p5-transcript-anchor-xfx.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
env TZ=UTC
work p5-transcript-ws
wait 4
type read and wait
wait 1
key Enter
wait 4
snap running
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-running
key PPage
wait 1
snap full-pgup
wait 10
snap full-pgup-after
key C-o
wait 1
key C-o
wait 2
snap full-end
key C-o
wait 1
snap end
gwlog
